  <compounddef id="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1failed__requirement" kind="struct" language="C++" prot="public">
    <compoundname>micro_os_plus::micro_test_plus::detail::failed_requirement</compoundname>
    <includes refid="check-result_8h" local="no">check-result.h</includes>
    <briefdescription>
<para>The exception thrown to stop a test case after a failed <computeroutput>require()</computeroutput>. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Thrown by the destructor of <computeroutput><ref refid="classmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1check__result" kindref="compound">check_result</ref></computeroutput>, after the failure was reported and counted, when exceptions are enabled, and caught by <computeroutput><ref refid="classmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1test__case_1adb4333ecb107fee477156b661f0b1512" kindref="member">test_case::run()</ref></computeroutput>, which ends the test case normally; the run continues with the next test case.</para>
<para>It is deliberately not derived from <computeroutput>std::exception</computeroutput>, so that a <computeroutput>catch (const std::exception&amp;)</computeroutput> in the test case body does not stop it; a <computeroutput>catch (...)</computeroutput> does, and should rethrow it. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
